{title: Masha the Doll}
{lyricist: Sergio Rykov}
{composer: Sergio Rykov}

{start_of_verse}
It happens so: she promises and leaves for nowhere.
She dissolves like a bird and melts without a trace.
She comes in a dream as a white cloud, a stream running down from the sky,
She runs after the firebird to wait for fleeting miracles.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
But here's the trouble —
Masha the doll keeps crying,
And throws herself headlong
Into the captivity of new feelings.
Leaving everywhere
Only the ashes of hope.
Running around in circles
And forgetting who we are.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse}
How long can I carefully choose the weave of words,
Afraid to disturb the fragile world around her.
Forgetting everything, again I hurry after her.
A trail of yellow haze drifts, vanishing in the distance.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
